    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds okay, but it feels a bit too \"middle of the road\" for a real policy brief. can u expand on the section about the risks of rapid phase-out? like, specifically what are the arguments that the economic instability and high costs are actually too big of a risk to justify the speed of the transition? i want to make sure the \"economic stability\" side isn't just treated as a minor hurdle but as a legitimate reason to slow down.",
